{
  "_contract": "docs/UC3/BUILD_CONTRACT.md (Phase A, binding). Companion: docs/UC3/FRAMEWORK_CAPABILITY_MAP.md",
  "_scenario": "UC3 Job 2 -- Excalibur streaming CDC. Reads the three staging tables the Job 1 simulator writes (flowx.staging.{physical_device,customer,subscriber}_stream) as Delta streams and applies SCD1/SCD2 CDC into the governed flowx.bronze layer, with framework-generated hash columns, null standardization, Unity Catalog governance tags and Iceberg read uniformity. Pure configuration -- no hand-written merge, hashing, nulling or tagging code exists or is needed (capability map section 1).",
  "_deviations_from_prompt": [
    "cdc_operation_mapping is {\"delete_values\": [\"1\"]}, NOT the contract's original guess {\"DELETE\": \"1\"}. spec_validator.py:1056-1059 requires delete_values as a list of strings and cdc/scd.py:92-95 evaluates it as F.col(op_column).isin(delete_values). BUILD_CONTRACT.md section 3 says the reference wins; the contract has since been corrected.",
    "Hash encoding is hex, not base64 -- cdc/hashing.py is the single canonical implementation and exposes no encoding switch (capability map 2.1).",
    "The hash column set is derived at runtime by resolve_comparison_columns, not enumerated in JSON; the per-flow _hash_specification key is the audit record (capability map 2.2).",
    "physical_device clusters on __framework_hash_key because its 4-column primary key exceeds MAX_LIQUID_CLUSTERING_COLUMNS = 3 (capability map 2.3). The PK is NOT truncated.",
    "UniForm emits one property (enable_iceberg_read_uniformity); delta.columnMapping.mode and delta.enableIcebergCompatV2 are set automatically by Databricks and cannot be forced, as table_properties is a closed key set (capability map 2.4).",
    "FlowX has no columns[] attribute; per-column concerns decompose into governance_tags.column_tags[] (capability map section 5)."
  ],
  "_src_deleted_flg_contract": "src_deleted_flg is materialized as STRING '1'/'0' by the Job 1 simulator (notebooks/uc3/simulator/uc3_ddl_schema.py: SRC_DELETED_FLG_TYPE = 'STRING') and by scripts/generate_uc3_test_data.py, even though the DDL sheets nominally type it BOOLEAN. delete_values must be a list of strings (check_list_of_str), and .isin(['1']) against a true BOOLEAN column would rely on implicit coercion. delete_values: ['1'] therefore matches the emitted data exactly. PHASE C VERIFICATION ITEM: confirm on the live staging table that src_deleted_flg is STRING-typed and that deleted rows carry '1'.",
  "dataflow_group_id": "dfg_uc3_excalibur_streaming_cdc",
